Login
This day, our team designed the Login screen for the Small Store Management app. You choose your role first, Admin or Cashier. Then you type your username and password. Tap Log In to enter the system. Each role sees only the tools it needs. This keeps your store data safe.
Dashboard
This day, our team designed the Dashboard. It shows your store's status for today. Today's Overview lists Total Sales, Total Utang, Transactions, and Profits in pesos. The Notice box shows reminders like low stock or unpaid utang. The bottom bar takes you to every screen. Tap Log Out at the top right when you finish.
Sells
This day, our team designed the Sells screen. You record each sale here. Type in the search bar to find a product fast. Tap a product card to add it to the sale. Each card shows the name and price, like Itlog at P10 or Canton at P22. Pick Cash or Utang as the payment type. For cash, type the amount received. Tap Charge to finish the sale.
Customer/Utang
This day, our team designed the Customer/Utang screen. It lists customers who owe you money. Each row shows the name and the amount owed. Juan Dela Cruz, Maria Antipolo, Mark Hernandez, and Marites Santos each owe P500. Tap Paid when a customer settles the debt. The list updates, so you always know who still owes you.
Products and Inventory Stocks
This day, our team designed the Products and Inventory Stocks screen. You add new items here. Type the name, price, stock count, and cost. Tap Add to save the item. The system uses these details in the Sells screen and in the Dashboard profit total. Check this screen often to keep your stock counts correct.


I. INTRODUCTION

 Background of the System

Small sari-sari store owners commonly manage sales, products, inventory, and customer credit manually. This can make it difficult to track daily sales and available stocks.

 

The POS and Inventory Management System will help store owners manage their products, sales, inventory, and customer credit records in one system.

Problem

Small shop owners may struggle to track daily sales, products stocks, and customer credit reccord. Manual recording can also cause and make it difficult to monitor the business.

Purpose of the System

The system is designed to help small sari-sari store owners manage sales, products, inventory, and customer credit more easily.

 Users of the System

Owner

· Manage products and inventory

· View sales and reports

· Manage cashier accounts

· Manage customer credit

Cashier

· Process customer purchases

· View products

· Record payments

· Record customer credit

Type of Application

Mobile Application

System Description

The system is a POS nad Inventory Management System for a Sari-sari store.

It allows the owner and casshier to process sales, manage products, monitor inventory, view sales records, and record customer credits.

II. System Requirements

1. Functional Requirements

1. The system should allow the owner and cashier to log in securely.

2. The owner can add, edit, and remove products.

3. The system automatically reduces the stock of the product when a sale is confirmed.

4. The cashier can process customer purchases.

5. The system calculates the total amount and the change.

6. The system logs the completed sale transactions.

7. The owner can see the sales reports daily and monthly.

